{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/747000-when-one-game-turns-into-other","id":747000,"title":"When one game turns into other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-01T10:23:49-08:00","id":747000,"title":"When one game turns into other?","content":"i been having this a lot of times with Hunter the Reckoning and Mage the ascension...how do you keep the feeling of both games separated?.<br /> i been intending to DM a sort of &quot;Mage the Ascension vs the Deadites.&quot; but it slowly feels like a HtR game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T11:42:39-08:00","id":747126,"title":"","content":"I would have just stuck as either HtR or Ascension. Hunter would be an alternate take on Evil Dead, while Mage would be Mage vs Earthbound Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T14:24:26-08:00","id":747457,"title":"","content":"The core of HtR is that the Imbued are underdogs. They have some nice powers, but they don't have the centuries of resources the other splats bring to play. The Evil Dead series is how HtR should generally look: a bunch of people doing a bit more than humans should be able to, up against something they don't really understand, and even if they can beat the minions are never really going to stand a chance to remove the evil power behind those monsters for good.<br /> <br /> Mages can solve the problem totally, but it's a matter of creativity instead of resources. Where the hunters are in a battle for outright survival against such an enemy, mages should be in for a battle of the minds. Can they outwit this demon so they can destroy its minions and kill it/banish it to the Deep beyond? It shouldn't every really be a question of, &quot;can we even do this?&quot; but, &quot;are we going to be smart enough about it to do it right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T16:57:28-08:00","id":747859,"title":"","content":"In this particular instance, as Heavy Arms notes I'd look at the characters themselves and the character types they come from. The Imbued have a small selection of abilities that they have to be creative with and little or no support network outside of the Net, while Mages have broader powers and potential membership of ancient secret societies (and enemies to match). Their approaches to fighting the same threat should be quite different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T23:13:32-08:00","id":748529,"title":"","content":"Is the problem you have both Imbued and Mages in the same group or that you are running Mages vs Zombies? I mean by itself Mages have all sorts of Temptations Hunters aren't. I mean for example the Zombie invasion may cause locallized reality zone shift, Mages deciding they can &quot;control&quot; the situation without destroying their Paradox free zone completely changes the whole scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:46:57-08:00","id":749470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/747000-when-one-game-turns-into-other#post747000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been having this a lot of times with Hunter the Reckoning and Mage the ascension...how do you keep the feeling of both games separated?.<br /> i been intending to DM a sort of &quot;Mage the Ascension vs the Deadites.&quot; but it slowly feels like a HtR game</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it feel like HtR game if the protagonists are Mages? Hunters are pretty limited in their power, comprehension and capability of dealing with the setting. The Mages can be more proactive and effective at dealing with threats. I'm not sure how those two things could change one into the other?<br /> <br /> If you have Mages who just happen to be badass monster hunters, that's normal for Mages, that's not playing Hunter The Reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:51:40-08:00","id":761837,"title":"","content":"that actually sounds like a really fun game, you need to have your players play up on their powers a bit more to pull it away from htr vibe, as mages they can tap untold powers that are limited only to their imaginations and how they fight should reflect that.<br /> <br /> I think we would need more information on the game itself, are the enemies superpowered, or have defences that negates the mages powers? Are the mage's powers limited in some way or were they depowered in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}